---@class posthog.visual_review.GetVisualReviewReposTolerationPileupRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string
---@field include_quarantined? boolean Keep snapshots that an active quarantine already covers. They are marked with `is_quarantined`. Set to false to see only piles nobody has acted on yet.
---@field limit? number Maximum number of snapshots to return. `total` and `truncated` say whether more matched.
---@field min_automatic_tolerations? number Also list a snapshot when it collected at least this many automatic tolerations in the window. An automatic toleration is a rendering under both diff thresholds, so it never blocked anybody; many of them still mean the story is unstable. Omit to ignore automatic tolerations when deciding what to list. With 10, the list matches the Tolerate dialog's quarantine suggestion.
---@field min_tolerations? number List a snapshot when a person or agent tolerated it at least this many times in the window. The default, 3, is the weekly debt digest's rule. Lower it to see snapshots that are starting to pile up, raise it to see only the worst ones.
---@field run_type? string Only list snapshots of this run type, for example `storybook` or `playwright`.
---@field window_days? number How many days back to count tolerations. Defaults to 30.

